.TH JOB-SCHEDULER 1 "" "job-scheduler" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
job-scheduler \- graphically manage cron jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B job-scheduler
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B job-scheduler
is a graphical utility for creating, editing, and removing scheduled tasks.
It reads and writes cron jobs through the system
.BR crontab (1)
command.
.PP
The application can manage the current user's crontab or, when started through
the privileged launcher, the root crontab and files in system cron directories.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/spool/cron/crontabs
System crontab spool directory on Debian-based systems.
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d
Directory containing system cron fragments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crontab (1),
.BR cron (8),
.BR job-scheduler-launcher (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by korewaisai, Adrian, and the MX Linux contributors.
